ORDERS - IMPLEMENTATION ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA

Scope definition
- Frontend viewer: on-screen app experience before purchase.
- Full Dossier/PDF: paid downloadable report.

1. Premium-only content visibility
- The following items must NOT be shown in the frontend viewer:
  - Asbestos Awareness
  - Soil Contamination Check
  - Shadow Snapshots
  - Direct sun (clear-sky visibility)
  - Property Warnings
  - Foundation Risk
- The same items MUST remain available in the paid Full Dossier/PDF output.
- Pass condition: these items are absent from viewer UI and present in Full Dossier/PDF generation.

2. Full Dossier purchase and download flow
- The user-visible entry point in the viewer is "Full Dossier".
- The "Buy Full Dossier" CTA is shown only after the user selects "Full Dossier".
- "Buy Full Dossier" must not be rendered in any other viewer location.
- Clicking "Buy Full Dossier" starts checkout/payment.
- After successful payment, the user can download the Full Dossier.
- Pass condition: no duplicate buy CTA in viewer, checkout starts from buy CTA, paid users can download dossier.

3. Viewing checklist CTA (single source of truth)
- Keep only one checklist download CTA in this section.
- Remove redundant "Download viewing checklist as PDF" text/button if a dedicated download button already exists below.
- The remaining checklist CTA/button label must clearly include "FREE".
- Clicking it downloads the viewing checklist as a PDF.
- Pass condition: exactly one checklist download CTA is visible, includes "FREE", and downloads PDF.

4. Remove redundant risk cards block
- Remove the risk cards block located between "Building Facts" and the street name section.
- Keep the main risk cards section that appears below (do not remove it).
- Pass condition: intermediate duplicate risk cards are gone; primary risk cards remain.

5. Neighborhood Snapshot text layout
- Cards: People, Housing, Accessibility.
- Text must not be truncated or clipped.
- Text should wrap to additional lines as needed.
- This must hold on mobile widths starting at 320px and larger.
- Pass condition: no cut-off labels/content on these cards across supported mobile breakpoints.
